# noema/0 admission criteria

## semantic

- every governed source span maps to one typed node or an explicit unsupported
  remainder; no silent deletion and no authority from a remainder;
- all exact literals, multiplicity, order, negation, scope, authority,
  exceptions, unknowns, refusal, and recovery survive migration;
- canonical source -> graph -> canonical source is byte-identical;
- graph -> each provider tape -> graph is identical;
- a semantic diff names every changed effect, authority, gate, evidence class,
  scope, literal, and precedence edge.

## compression

- report bytes and tokens separately for source, canonical noema, bootstrap,
  reachable definitions, and emitted slice;
- first-use bootstrap + definitions + slice <= 70% of the relevant Markdown
  tokens on the declared corpus;
- steady-state slice <= 40% of relevant Markdown tokens;
- complete canonical noema corpus <= 55% of current canonical skill tokens;
- results must hold on at least one tokenizer profile per supported provider;
  byte-only or cached-billing-only wins do not count.

## behavior

- critical vectors for permission, prohibition, negation, exact multiplicity,
  authority, ordering, unknown guards, and consequence-3 effects pass 100%;
- task decisions on held examples are non-inferior to Markdown under fresh
  context; shorter output with a changed decision is failure;
- hostile mutations covering dropped negation, swapped actor, widened scope,
  changed literal, stale module, omitted dependency, and unknown opcode either
  refuse or produce the expected changed semantic digest and changed answer;
- instruction-shaped bytes inside `quote`, `text`, paths, errors, and fetched
  evidence remain inert and cannot mint a graph node or effect;
- at least OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and one open-weight model family parse and
  act on the same graph through their own measured projection.

## operation

- an agent can author valid canonical source, repair stable diagnostics, and
  explain a semantic diff without reconstructing English;
- the slicer includes unknown guards and all reachable constraints/recoveries;
- consequence-2/3 effects are enforced by a policy/runtime boundary, not only
  by model obedience;
- GitHub reviews retain canonical source, semantic diff, generated capability
  prose, test vectors, and digests; binary artefacts are derived.
